**Definition 1.5 (completion).** Write $\widehat{\mathcal T}$ for all valid
finite or infinite full ordered binary trees with $\alpha/\beta$ leaves and
the same four replies. It is the compact closed valid-tree subspace of the
countable four-reply product and is complete for the prefix metric. A finite
tree is isolated by its replies through its maximum leaf depth. Every finite
valid prefix has a finite filling. The unique leafless tree is $\Omega$.
The extended $\rho$ uses exactly (NIS.1). Fixed powers are prefix nonexpanding,
infinite branches persist, and $\rho$ is injective on this completion
[SFS, Lemma 2.1][SFS]. Pairing gains one agreement depth. Guarded recursion
below uses that explicit pair gain; bare $\rho$ has no assumed contraction.

